(a) The city may adopt charges and fees for the following:
(1) Fees for reimbursement of costs of setting up and operating a pretreatment program;
(2) Fees for monitoring, inspections and surveillance procedures;
(3) Fees for reviewing accidental discharge procedures and construction;
(4) Fees for filing appeals;
(5) Fees as the city may deem necessary to carry out the requirements contained herein; and
(6) Fees for holding or septic tank waste.
(b) These fees relate solely to the matters covered by this division and are separate from all other fees chargeable by the city.
(Ord. of 7-19-2004, § 5)
